{#
  THE ABOUT -> TESTIMONIALS SUPERSECTION — Figma 664:61547, 666:61738, 673:1638.

  ONE SECTION, ONE PINNED BAND, FOUR LAYERS. This was two sections with two
  sticky stages, and being two was the bug: the second section's own background
  painted a 60px band between the photos and flipped the ±120 page margins from
  white to black at the join. There is nothing to align here because there is
  nothing to join — one band is pinned for the whole sequence and the content
  flows over it.

  THE FOUR LAYERS, in paint order:
    story__shot--about    the About photo + its dim (0 -> 0.82)      z 0
    story__shot--testi    the Testimonials photo + its 0.55 dim      z 1
    story__layer--about   the About text, clipped at the TOP only    z 2
    story__layer--testi   the cards, clipped top AND bottom          z 3

  THE PANELS ARE display:contents WHILE PINNED, which is what lets that flat
  order exist. Pairing each photo with its content is what the static regime
  needs — two stacked blocks, each a photo backing its own copy — but a real box
  around the pair would be a stacking context, and the four layers could no
  longer interleave. display:contents dissolves the box under the pin and brings
  it back below 900, so one markup serves both.

  THE ASYMMETRIC CROSSFADE. The About shot stays fully opaque and the
  Testimonials shot fades in OVER it, each carrying its own dim inside the layer
  that fades. Two layers fading in opposite directions would dip at the halfway
  point — 50% of each over the page — and the band would flash lighter mid
  transition. This way the composite is opaque at every frame.

  THE BEATS, in scroll pixels down the 1478px runway:
    A     0.00 ->  678.86   About text rises 797.73 -> 118.87; its dim 0 -> 0.82
    B   678.86 -> 1318.46   About text rises on to -520.73 and off the top
    x   797.73 -> 1117.73   the photo crossfades, About -> Testimonials
    C   797.73 -> 1318.46   the cards rise 757.73 -> 237 and settle
    hold 1318.46 -> 1478.00 nothing moves — reading time, and a still window for
                            the card scroller
    D  past 1478.00         the stage releases; band and cards leave together

  BEAT C STARTS ON THE FRAME THE ABOUT TEXT'S TOP EDGE CROSSES THE BAND'S TOP
  EDGE. Both land on 797.73, and that is not a coincidence to be maintained by
  hand: About needs 639.60 to clear, the cards need 520.73 to arrive, and
  offsetting them by the 118.87 the text is sitting at makes the last of the old
  copy leave as the first of the new content settles.

  #about-me IS ON THE SECTION, not on the About layer. It is the nav anchor and
  the element analytics-events.js observes for view_about, and it belongs on the
  box that spans the whole sequence. data-header-theme likewise: parallax.js
  flips it dark at 0.160758, which is the same 237.60 scroll pixels the About-only
  version flipped at.
#}

<section
  class="story"
  id="about-me"
  data-header-theme="light"
  data-parallax="--story-progress"
  data-parallax-flip="0.160758"
>

  <div class="story__stage">

    <div class="story__panel story__panel--about">
      {#- aria-hidden with an empty alt: the photo is atmosphere, and the three
          paragraphs beside it already say everything it says. -#}
      <div class="story__shot story__shot--about" aria-hidden="true">
        <img
          class="story__photo"
          src="{{ about.photo.file }}"
          alt=""
          width="1600"
          height="2844"
          decoding="async"
          draggable="false"
        />
        <div class="story__dim story__dim--about"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="story__layer story__layer--about">
        {% include "partials/about.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="story__panel story__panel--testi">
      {#- Pari at the Mindful Meet poster session. Atmosphere again — nothing in
          it is information the three quotes do not already carry. -#}
      <div class="story__shot story__shot--testi" aria-hidden="true">
        <img
          class="story__photo story__photo--testi"
          src="/Assets/images/testimonials/testimonials.jpg"
          alt=""
          width="1200"
          height="1600"
          decoding="async"
          loading="lazy"
          draggable="false"
        />
        <div class="story__dim story__dim--testi"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="story__layer story__layer--testi">
        {% include "partials/testimonials.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>{#- /.story__stage -#}

  {#- THE SUB-ANCHOR, AND IT IS A MARKER RATHER THAN AN id ON THE CARDS. The card
      layer lives inside the sticky stage, so its offsetTop is the stage's and
      jumping to it would land the reader at the very start of the About
      sequence. This box sits in the runway at exactly the offset where the cards
      settle, so #testimonials scrolls to the frame it names. -#}
  <div id="testimonials" class="story__anchor" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {#- THE PIN'S SCROLL DISTANCE. A real element for the same reason .hero__runway
      and .work__runway are: padding sits outside the content box a sticky child
      is bounded by, so only a sibling with height can extend the pin. Its height
      IS the travel — parallax.js measures this box, not the section. -#}
  <div class="story__runway" data-parallax-runway aria-hidden="true"></div>
</section>
